gher in AD","nucleus_padj":0.942558,"nucleus_log2fc":0.0486453,"nucleus_score":0.203736,"pct_ad":0.118081,"pct_control":0.114856,"donor_test":"not tested","donor_padj":null,"donor_log2fc":null,"donor_lfcse":null,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":null},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"ITPR1","gene_symbol_current":"ITPR1","gene_id":"ENSG00000150995","nucleus_tested":false,"nucleus_significant":null,"nucleus_direction":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.902484,"donor_log2fc":0.123408,"donor_lfcse":0.172248,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.0042106}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"Ast","gene_id":"ENSG00000150995","module":"red","kme":0.165359,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.32433,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Ex","gene_id":"ENSG00000150995","module":"blue","kme":0.320667,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.474279,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"In","gene_id":"ENSG00000150995","module":"brown","kme":0.285691,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.372712,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000150995","entrez_id":["3708"],"uniprot":["Q14643"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes an intracellular receptor for inositol 1,4,5-trisphosphate. Upon stimulation by inositol 1,4,5-trisphosphate, this receptor mediates calcium release from the endoplasmic reticulum. Mutations in this gene cause spinocerebellar ataxia type 15, a disease associated with an heterogeneous group of cerebellar disorders. Multiple transcript variants have been identified for this gene. [provided by RefSeq, Nov 2009].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q14643","text":"Inositol 1,4,5-trisphosphate-gated calcium channel that, upon inositol 1,4,5-trisphosphate binding, mediates calcium release from the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) (PubMed:10620513, PubMed:27108797). Undergoes conformational changes upon ligand binding, suggesting structural flexibility that allows the channel to switch from a closed state, capable of interacting with its ligands such as 1,4,5-trisphosphate and calcium, to an open state, capable of transferring calcium ions across the ER membrane (By similarity). Cytoplasmic calcium released from the ER triggers apoptosis by the activation of CAMK2 complex (By similarity). Involved in the regulation of epithelial secretion of electrolytes and fluid through the interaction with AHCYL1 (By similarity). Part of a complex composed of HSPA9, ITPR1 and VDAC1 that regulates mitochondrial calcium-dependent apoptosis by facilitating calcium transport from the ER lumen to the mitochondria intermembrane space thus providing calcium for the downstream calcium channel MCU that directly releases it into mitochondria matrix (By similarity). Regulates fertilization and egg activation by tuning the frequency and amplitude of calcium oscillations (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}